# Entry point. Everything else is an include, so a machine gets host
# definitions by which files its profile links, not by editing this file.
#
# OpenSSH takes the FIRST value it sees for each keyword, so include order is
# precedence order. The three directories below encode that:
#
#   local.d     machine-local, never tracked. First, so it wins over anything
#               managed. Put hosts here that should not be in a public repo.
#   config.d    managed host definitions, one file per site. Numbered only to
#               keep the listing stable; the files do not overlap, so the
#               order among them does not actually matter.
#   platform.d  Host * blocks. Last, so every specific host above wins.
#
# A glob that matches nothing is not an error, so a missing directory is fine.

Include ~/.ssh/local.d/*
Include ~/.ssh/config.d/*
Include ~/.ssh/platform.d/*
